        "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued June 6 at 12:58PM AKDT until June 8 at 10:00PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Snow expected. Total snow accumulations between 5 and 10\ninches. Winds gusting as high as 30 mph at Atigun Pass.\n\n* WHERE...Central Brooks Range.\n\n* WHEN...From 10 PM this evening to 10 PM AKDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult. Gusty winds could lead to\nareas of blowing snow which could significantly reduce visibility.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...An unseasonably strong arctic trough will\npass over the North Slope and Brooks Range Sunday into Monday.\nWidespread light snow is ex",
